WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.253
This guide uses the running app with fictional training records.

5
00:00:04.253 --> 00:00:07.404
Camera, location and cloud responses are simulated.

9
00:00:07.404 --> 00:00:10.369
Sign in with your company username and password.

13
00:00:10.369 --> 00:00:13.643
The written guide includes every task and setup step.

17
00:00:14.443 --> 00:00:17.424
The overview shows activity and review stages.

21
00:00:17.424 --> 00:00:21.636
N P I can inspect every permitted company, assignment and worker.

25
00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:27.597
Subcontractors manage their daily scheduling; N P I monitors evidence and verifies the work.

29
00:00:28.397 --> 00:00:32.379
Add the subcontractor company, locations and services first.

33
00:00:32.379 --> 00:00:36.627
Register the main contract and assign its sites to that company.

37
00:00:36.627 --> 00:00:38.817
Repeat for future subcontractors.

41
00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:42.866
No rates or invoices are included in this operations release.

45
00:00:43.666 --> 00:00:47.165
Invite the company administrator from People and access.

49
00:00:47.165 --> 00:00:51.477
Select the correct company and create its single-use, seven-day link.

53
00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:52.664
Share it privately.

57
00:00:52.664 --> 00:01:00.226
The administrator chooses their credentials and invites their own workers; N P I does not need to know the workers first.

61
00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:05.444
Locations shows the supplied building pictures and verified addresses.

65
00:01:05.444 --> 00:01:11.062
Add access instructions, hazards and optional site coordinates for advisory G P S checks.

69
00:01:11.062 --> 00:01:17.059
In Settings, configure whether each service needs before and after pictures on new assignments.

73
00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:20.260
Work orders is the shared register.

77
00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.239
Filter by contract, company, site, worker, date or status.

81
00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:27.601
Every card shows the assignment creator and team.

85
00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:32.883
Open a record to inspect each worker’s attendance and the assignment history.

89
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:37.331
Compare recorded, claimed and accepted hours separately.

93
00:01:37.331 --> 00:01:41.827
Inspect check in and checkout times, captured positions and accuracy.

97
00:01:41.827 --> 00:01:44.564
A map link opens the recorded coordinates.

101
00:01:44.564 --> 00:01:50.362
Location flags need investigation; they do not automatically prove that work was invalid.

105
00:01:51.162 --> 00:01:57.168
The grouped gallery shows the worker’s before, after and issue pictures from this training transaction.

109
00:01:57.168 --> 00:02:00.433
Check who uploaded each file and the server upload time.

113
00:02:00.433 --> 00:02:03.348
Capture or preparation stamps are device-reported.

117
00:02:03.348 --> 00:02:05.680
Open the unchanged original when needed.

121
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.992
After company approval, choose Verify and accept hours.

125
00:02:09.992 --> 00:02:13.249
Keep exact claimed hours or explain any adjustment.

129
00:02:13.249 --> 00:02:17.208
Review incomplete outcomes and evidence exceptions explicitly.

133
00:02:17.208 --> 00:02:21.997
If information is missing, return the work with a useful correction reason.

137
00:02:22.797 --> 00:02:27.840
Settings contains N P I’s own recipient list and urgent acknowledgement deadline.

141
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.891
Each company maintains its recipients separately.

145
00:02:30.891 --> 00:02:34.689
Test delivery after the owner configures the verified sender.

149
00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:39.545
The queue distinguishes queued, retry, failed and accepted-by-provider states.

153
00:02:40.345 --> 00:02:44.137
Alerts shows assignments, issue reports and review updates.

157
00:02:44.137 --> 00:02:47.608
Issues tracks responsibility, comments and resolution.

161
00:02:47.608 --> 00:02:51.335
Both N P I and the relevant company receive issue notices.

165
00:02:51.335 --> 00:02:56.091
Private photos stay behind sign-in and are not attached publicly to email.

169
00:02:56.891 --> 00:02:59.932
The compact management workbook has seven tabs.

173
00:02:59.932 --> 00:03:02.585
Operational records mirror from Supabase.

177
00:03:02.585 --> 00:03:07.180
Permitted planning and site edits return as proposals for N P I review.

181
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.156
Check the values and version before accepting.

185
00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:14.104
Original attendance, evidence and approvals remain protected.

189
00:03:14.904 --> 00:03:19.163
Activity reports highlight exceptions and export the loaded records.

193
00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:22.420
The work register searches older records with pages.

197
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:32.004
Before rollout, apply the backend upgrade, configure email delivery and workbook triggers, deploy the frontend and complete a real phone acceptance test.
